
ARC desktop unit tests
======================

These tests compile the real library headers with small ESP-IDF/FreeRTOS
test doubles. No board, serial connection, PlatformIO package download, or
third-party test framework is required. A C++20 desktop compiler and CMake
3.16+ are required (I2CBus uses unordered_map::contains).

Run from the repository root in a compiler-enabled terminal, for example
the Visual Studio Developer PowerShell or Developer Command Prompt:

    cmake -S test -B test/build -G "NMake Makefiles" -DCMAKE_BUILD_TYPE=Debug
    cmake --build test/build
    cd test/build
    ctest --output-on-failure

For Linux/macOS, omit the -G "NMake Makefiles" option. For a Visual Studio
generator, also supply --config Debug when building and -C Debug to ctest.
Run arc_unit_tests.exe directly in the build folder to see each named case
(Visual Studio generators place it in the Debug subfolder).
Failures return a nonzero exit code, including in Release builds.

This is a standalone CMake project, not a PlatformIO test environment.
The root CMake project remains ESP-IDF. The build folder is ignored by Git.
On this Windows installation, CMake and CTest are also available under
C:/pio-user/packages/tool-cmake/bin if they are not on PATH.

Coverage targets and cases
-------------------------
* Vec3: arithmetic, cross/dot products, length/angle, normalization,
  projection/reflection, interpolation, clamping, casts, and zero vectors.
* RS485Utils: big-endian U32 decoding at offsets, zero and high-bit values.
* i2cUtils: little-endian signed I16 decoding, including both signed limits.
* SensorUtils: every defined status string.
* LockGuard: one release after acquisition, no release for null/failed
  acquisition, exception cleanup, and compile-time copy prevention.
* I2CBus: bus/mux configuration, duplicate and missing names, register
  framing, read results, correct device selection, channel boundaries,
  and propagation of injected setup/transfer errors.

These are unit tests, not timing or electrical validation. Test doubles
record arguments and inject failures; they do not simulate an RTOS or bus.
No line-coverage percentage is claimed.

Remaining coverage gaps
-----------------------
app_main currently contains only an infinite loop. Sensor task lifecycle,
optical preconfiguration, invalid mux indices, failed sensor-registration
rollback, and the private RS485 packet parser are not covered by this suite.
Parser coverage needs a callable byte-input/result interface or a dedicated
parser unit. Hardware integration tests should separately verify UART
framing/checksum recovery, I2C mux isolation, real sensor readings, task
scheduling, and lock contention on the ESP32-S3.
